      "id": 56298,
      "name": "smafdi",
      "username": "smafdi",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/c67d28/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-03-22T15:31:49.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>No, putting a card into play gets around situations just like Two Left Feet. When you play a card you are putting it into play, but the reverse is not true. Putting a card into play is not the same as playing a card. They both give you the same end result, but get around some shenanigans like hero's cannot play cards.</p>",
